  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraqi Federation of Industries (IFI) is actively working and providing support to the different ILO initiatives in the country.  As part of the ILO activities in the country, an Enabling Environment for Sustainable Enterprise (EESE)  assessment is being undertaken focusing on women and fragile situations. At the same time, ILO aims to support formalization efforts in the country. 
As an incentive to tackle informality, the Government of Iraq recently passed social protection law establishing that all workers need to be enrolled and insured in all branches of social security, including health, and extends coverage to self-employed workers (through optional insurance) and workers in the informal economy. This opens the way to define and promote enterprise formalization pathways and include specific supporting services offered by IFI and support their capacity to engage with their members and outreach new members.</narrative>
  </description>
